       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The FDA-labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day. Most guidance uses 2,000 mg/day for immediate-release tablets. The order is about twice the labeled maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. This applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n1700 mg may be a typo. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1700 mg total per day, divided into doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
